<title>UK: Siebe gains on Electrolux deal.</title>
<headline>Siebe gains on Electrolux deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British diversified engineering group Siebe rose over one percent on Friday after the company said it agreed a deal with Sweden's Electrolux to supply refrigerator and freezer controls.</p>
<p>News of the deal, worth over 40 million pounds over three years, helped Siebe shares to an intraday high of 958p before they settled back at 957p in early trade, up 12p on the day.</p>
<p>Volumes were modest, with 49,852 shares changing hands.</p>
<p>Siebe is the world's largest manufacturer of domestic and commercial appliance controls.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
